 "why_the_numbers_differ": [
  "Counting rule (same data): 'linked' counts any row; the new rule counts consumption separately. On main's catalog the new rule gives 952 linked / 856 consumption / 810 consumption checked in the original / 91 reference only.",
  "91 taxa are linked only through wild_diet_not_detected / offered_not_eaten / toxicity / nutrition rows (e.g. Anacyclus radiatus, El Mouden et al. 2006: present in habitat, absent from 44 faeces). They do not count as consumption.",
  "5 taxa are linked only through husbandry recommendations (care-sheet advice, not an observed feeding); counted separately.",
  "Of the 858 consumption taxa, 46 have no consumption row checked in the original (abstract 9, automatic extraction 5, unverified literature lead 6, community/video 26). 'Checked in the original' is the builder's own set (CHECKED_LEVELS).",
  "New data in this branch: 7 evidence rows read in the original and promoted (Wagle et al. 2026, 6 rows for Indotestudo elongata; Rodrigues & Oliveira 2016, 1 row for Chelonoidis carbonarius). Two plants gained their first consumption record: Abelmoschus esculentus and Bombax ceiba (captive I. elongata).",
  "Public research status: reference-only taxa had evidence_checked_in_full_text ('원문으로 확인한 급여 기록 있음'); they now get the existing status reviewed_not_feeding_evidence ('거북 문헌에 이름은 나오지만 먹이 기록은 아님'). evidence_checked_in_full_text 907 -> 818, reviewed_not_feeding_evidence 4 -> 95. Label texts unchanged."
 ],
